### Limitation of the definition

An active thread can have a large subdivision load even if only its endpoint remains unburned. Conversely, a residual component can meet only core vertices. Therefore, counting active threads is not itself a charging argument.

A successful lemma must establish a new relationship between the residual burning obstruction and the subdivision loads of the active threads.

